{"name":"Canary Island","hex":"#e9d4a9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Canary Island","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An island of the Canary Islands."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Attributive form of Canary Islands.","A locality in the Shire of Loddon, north western Victoria, Australia."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Canary_Island"}],"entries":[{"title":"Canary Islands","blocks":[{"text":"The Canary Islands or Canaries are an archipelago in the Atlantic Ocean and the southernmost autonomous community of Spain, located about 100 kilometres (60 mi) off the northwest coast of Africa. The archipelago has a population of approximately 2.27 million inhabitants, making it the most populous overseas special territory of the European Union."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Flag_of_the_Canary_Islands.svg/330px-Flag_of_the_Canary_Islands.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canary_Islands","wikidata":"Q5813"},{"title":"Island","blocks":[{"text":"An island or isle is a piece of land, distinct from a continent, completely surrounded by water. There are continental islands, which were formed by being split from a continent by plate tectonics, and oceanic islands, which have never been part of a continent. Oceanic islands can be formed from volcanic activity, grow into atolls from coral reefs, and form from sediment along shorelines, creating barrier islands. River islands can also form from sediment and debris in rivers. Artificial islands are those made by humans, including small rocky outcroppings built out of lagoons and large-scale land reclamation projects used for development."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Hawaje-NoRedLine.jpg/330px-Hawaje-NoRedLine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wi